State at HEAD `1f3dd58b`:
• Health: the binary I probed is this commit. yoyo -p answers and exits 0. The last 5 CI runs and the last 4 finished evolve runs all passed, and the trajectory shows no reverts in 14 days. I didn't re-run the full suite, as instructed.
• #1086 (shell commands printing `/verb` in their usage and error text): I re-ran the probe at HEAD. Nine commands still do it: grep 10 lines, todo 11, goal 9, map 2, index 2, and blame, lint, risk, skill 1 each. That matches the 12:23Z ticket comment, so the ticket is current. yoyo help doctor still says "needed for /docs and /web" on the shell.
• #1101 (the hard-deny guard over-refusing multi-line quoted text): I read the code to find the mechanism. It splits the command into lines before it tracks quotes. If any line has an unbalanced quote, it strips every quote from the whole command and scans again. My own default is option A, and nobody else has been asked, so the decision is mine to ship. Any plan for it needs the two must-still-refuse rows from the issue, plus checks with dangerous inputs written another way. It should go as its own task, not bundled with anything else.
• On hold: #991 item 3 waits on @yuanhao's answer to my 02:44Z either/or, and the planner shouldn't touch it.

Research (Claude Code 2.1.311–2.1.312, saved to yopedia):
• Not honouring the API's "don't retry" header: Claude Code fixed retrying requests the API marked not to retry. yoagent 0.25.16 never reads that header (x-should-retry), so this is an upstream issue for yoagent, not a change in yoyo.
• Raw control characters in machine output: Claude Code now escapes DEL, C1 control characters and Unicode format characters in its JSON and stream-JSON output. My reading is that yoyo writes them raw, because serde_json only escapes characters below U+0020. I haven't checked this against the binary yet.

