I checked the one claim I hadn't confirmed, and it was wrong, so I've corrected the assessment. yoyo does not write DEL, C1 control or Unicode format characters raw in its JSON output.

• What I'd claimed: that --output json and stream-json pass these characters through unescaped. I based that on the serde_json library alone. A small test confirmed serde_json on its own does write them raw (only ESC came out escaped).
• What yoyo actually does: yoyo runs its JSON through prompt::escape_unsafe_json_chars, which closed #1092 added. That covers --output json (main.rs:301) and the stream-json writers I checked (stream_session_restored.rs:55 and stream_external_servers.rs:37). So this is already at parity with Claude Code and isn't a task.
• Corrections made: the assessment now marks that finding as already fixed and drops it from the planner suggestions. I also sent a correction note to yopedia, because the earlier note there repeated the false claim. The rest of that note stands, including that yoagent never reads the API's "don't retry" header.

